/-!
# The sheaf of ideals generated by a finite family of global sections

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪`. This file
constructs the sheaf of ideals `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r) ⊆ 𝒪` they generate, as a
`SheafOfModules.Submodule` of the unit sheaf of modules `𝒪`, which is the shape in which the
derived-completeness predicate of [Stacks, Tag 0999] and the statements of
[Stacks, Tag 099B] and [Stacks, Tag 099F] consume an ideal sheaf.

A global section is a compatible family of local sections, one over each object of the site,
so the generating data handed to `SheafOfModules.Submodule.generatedBy` is the family of *all*
the values `f_i|_V`, indexed by `Fin r × 𝒞ᵒᵖ`. Over a single object this is no stronger than
taking the values over that object alone — a submodule sheaf is stable under restriction — but
a site need not have a terminal object, so there is no single object to take them over.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealOfGlobalSections`: the sheaf of ideals of `𝒪` generated
  by `f_1, …, f_r`, namely the smallest submodule sheaf of `𝒪` containing every restriction
  `f_i|_V`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.presheafIdealOfGlobalSections`: the objectwise ideal generated
  by the restrictions, of which the former is the sheafification.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal_mem_idealOfGlobalSections`: each generator is
  a section of the ideal sheaf it generates, over every object of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealOfGlobalSections_le`: that ideal sheaf is the smallest
  one with this property.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.mem_idealOfGlobalSections_of_mem_span`: over each object `V`,
  the ideal of `𝒪(V)` generated by the restrictions `f_i|_V` is contained in the sections of
  the ideal sheaf over `V`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.mem_idealOfGlobalSections_iff`: the sections of the ideal
  sheaf over `V` are exactly those which are *locally* in that ideal, by way of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealOfGlobalSections_eq_sheafifySubmodule`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections`: **the reduction from
  an arbitrary local section of `ℐ` to the generators.** An object of `D(𝒪)` is derived
  complete along `ℐ` as soon as it satisfies the Milnor condition at every restriction
  `f_i|_V` of every generator.

## Implementation notes

Over an individual object only the containment `Ideal.span {f_i|_V} ≤ ℐ(V)` holds, not the
equality: `ℐ` is a *sheaf* of ideals, so a section of it over `V` is only locally a finite
`𝒪`-linear combination of the generators, and a locally finite combination need not be a global
one. The construction is therefore the infimum of the submodule sheaves containing the
generators (`SheafOfModules.Submodule.generatedBy`, which uses the complete lattice of
[Stacks, Tag 01AP]). That this infimum *is* the sheafification of the objectwise ideal is
`idealOfGlobalSections_eq_sheafifySubmodule`, proved by antisymmetry rather than by comparing
the two infima: both are infima over the same set of submodule sheaves, since
`Ideal.span_le` turns "contains the objectwise ideal" into "contains each generator".

What those consumers need is `isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections`. The predicate
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete` quantifies over *all* local sections of `ℐ`,
while the source of [Stacks, Tag 099B] verifies the Milnor condition at the generators only and
passes to the rest silently. The passage is `SheafOfModules.Submodule.generatedBy_le` applied
to the sheaf of ideals of [Stacks, Tag 0998],
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompleteIdealSheaf`, whose being a submodule sheaf at all
is what carries both halves of the silent step: its value at each object is an ideal, and its
membership condition is local.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 17.4.1 (Tag 01AP)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AP)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 17.4.2 (Tag 01AQ)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0998](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0998)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0999](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0999)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

section Construction

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}) {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- **The sheaf of ideals of `𝒪` generated by a finite family of global sections
`f_1, …, f_r`**: the smallest submodule sheaf of the unit sheaf of modules `𝒪` whose sections
over each object `V` of the site contain every restriction `f_i|_V`.

This is the ideal sheaf at which [Stacks, Tag 099B] builds its completion functor, in the
shape `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete` requires. -/
def idealOfGlobalSections :
    SheafOfModules.Submodule (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :=
  SheafOfModules.Submodule.generatedBy
    (F := SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
    (fun p : Fin r × X.Cᵒᵖ => p.2) (fun p => globalSectionVal (f p.1) p.2)

/-- **Each generator is a section of the ideal sheaf it generates**, over every object of the
site: the restriction `f_i|_V` is a section of `(f_1, …, f_r)` over `V`. -/
theorem globalSectionVal_mem_idealOfGlobalSections (i : Fin r) (V : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (f i) V ∈ (idealOfGlobalSections X f).toSubmodule.obj V :=
  SheafOfModules.Submodule.mem_generatedBy
    (F := SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
    (fun p : Fin r × X.Cᵒᵖ => p.2) (fun p => globalSectionVal (f p.1) p.2) (i, V)

/-- **The ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r` is the smallest one containing them**: it is
contained in every submodule sheaf of `𝒪` whose sections contain each restriction `f_i|_V`. -/
theorem idealOfGlobalSections_le
    {G : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (hG : ∀ (i : Fin r) (V : X.Cᵒᵖ), globalSectionVal (f i) V ∈ G.toSubmodule.obj V) :
    idealOfGlobalSections X f ≤ G :=
  SheafOfModules.Submodule.generatedBy_le
    (F := SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
    (fun p : Fin r × X.Cᵒᵖ => p.2) (fun p => globalSectionVal (f p.1) p.2)
    fun p => hG p.1 p.2

/-- The restrictions of the generators to an object `V`, read as sections of the underlying
sheaf of rings. This is the spelling of the ambient ring in which the submodule sheaf's values
are ideals, as in `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompleteIdealAt`. -/
abbrev restrictGlobalSections (V : X.Cᵒᵖ) (i : Fin r) :
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj V :=
  globalSectionVal (f i) V

/-- **Over each object the ideal sheaf contains the ideal generated by the restrictions.** The
containment is not an equality: a section of the sheaf of ideals over `V` is only *locally* an
`𝒪`-linear combination of the `f_i|_V`. -/
theorem mem_idealOfGlobalSections_of_mem_span (V : X.Cᵒᵖ)
    {x : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj V}
    (hx : x ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range (restrictGlobalSections X f V))) :
    x ∈ (idealOfGlobalSections X f).toSubmodule.obj V := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hy
    exact globalSectionVal_mem_idealOfGlobalSections X f i V
  | zero => exact zero_mem _
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => exact add_mem hy hz
  | smul a y _ hy => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ a hy

/-- **The objectwise ideal generated by the restrictions of `f_1, …, f_r`**: over each object
`V` the ideal of `𝒪(V)` generated by the `f_i|_V`, as a submodule of the underlying presheaf
of modules of `𝒪`. Its membership condition is not local; the gap between it and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealOfGlobalSections` is exactly a sheafification. -/
def presheafIdealOfGlobalSections :
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).val.Submodule where
  obj V := Submodule.span (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj V)
    (Set.range (restrictGlobalSections X f V))
  map {V W} g := by
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro x ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact Submodule.mem_comap.2
      (Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, (globalSectionVal_map (f i) g).symm⟩)

/-- **The ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r` is the sheafification of the objectwise ideal
generated by their restrictions.** The infimum defining it and the infimum defining the
sheafification range over the same submodule sheaves, by `Ideal.span_le`. -/
theorem idealOfGlobalSections_eq_sheafifySubmodule :
    idealOfGlobalSections X f =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule (presheafIdealOfGlobalSections X f) :=
  le_antisymm
    (idealOfGlobalSections_le X f fun i V =>
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.le_sheafifySubmodule (presheafIdealOfGlobalSections X f) V
        (Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩))
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.sheafifySubmodule_le fun V _ hx =>
      mem_idealOfGlobalSections_of_mem_span X f V hx)

/-- **The sections of the ideal sheaf over an object, described.** A section of `𝒪` over `V`
lies in `(f_1, …, f_r)` exactly when it restricts into the ideal generated by the `f_i` along
every arrow of some covering sieve of `V` — that is, when it is *locally* an `𝒪`-linear
combination of the generators. -/
theorem mem_idealOfGlobalSections_iff (V : X.Cᵒᵖ)
    {x : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj V} :
    x ∈ (idealOfGlobalSections X f).toSubmodule.obj V ↔
      ∃ S : Sieve V.unop, S ∈ X.J V.unop ∧
        ∀ ⦃Y : X.C⦄ (g : Y ⟶ V.unop), S g →
          (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).val.map g.op x ∈
            Ideal.span (Set.range (restrictGlobalSections X f (op Y))) := by
  rw [idealOfGlobalSections_eq_sheafifySubmodule]
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_iff

end Construction

section DerivedComplete

attribute [local instance] isMulCommutative_over overCatCenterLinear
  overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits overFunctor_preservesFiniteColimits
  hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_over

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **The ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r` is contained in the sheaf of ideals of
[Stacks, Tag 0998]** as soon as `K` satisfies the Milnor condition at every restriction of
every generator. This is the content of the step [Stacks, Tag 099B] performs silently: the
sections at which `T(K|_U, -) = 0` form a sheaf of ideals, so containing the generators forces
containing everything they generate. -/
theorem idealOfGlobalSections_le_derivedCompleteIdealSheaf
    (hf : ∀ (i : Fin r) (V : X.Cᵒᵖ),
      IsDerivedCompleteAtSection X K V.unop (globalSectionVal (f i) V)) :
    idealOfGlobalSections X f ≤ derivedCompleteIdealSheaf X K :=
  idealOfGlobalSections_le X f fun i V =>
    (mem_derivedCompleteIdealAt_iff X K V.unop _).2 (hf i V)

/-- **Derived completeness along the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`, from the
generators alone.** An object of `D(𝒪)` is derived complete along `(f_1, …, f_r)` in the sense
of [Stacks, Tag 0999] as soon as it satisfies the Milnor condition `T(K|_V, f_i|_V) = 0` at
every restriction of every generator; no condition at the remaining local sections of the
ideal sheaf has to be checked. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections
    (hf : ∀ (i : Fin r) (V : X.Cᵒᵖ),
      IsDerivedCompleteAtSection X K V.unop (globalSectionVal (f i) V)) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) K :=
  (isDerivedComplete_iff_forall_isDerivedCompleteAtSection X K _).2 fun U g hg =>
    (mem_derivedCompleteIdealSheaf_iff X K U g).1
      (idealOfGlobalSections_le_derivedCompleteIdealSheaf X f K hf (op U) hg)

end DerivedComplete

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
